<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21682" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immātūrĭtas</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inm-</span></b> ),
			ātis, f.
		immaturus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Unripeness</i>, <i>immatureness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sponsarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 34</span></i>
			.—*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Untimely haste</i>, <i>over-eagerness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid haec festinatio, quid haec immaturitas
					tanta significat?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Quint. 26, 82</span></i>
			.</div>
